<given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Mazzaferri</surname><given-names>EL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Familial adenomatous polyposis (Gardner&#x02019;s syndrome) and thyroid carcinoma - A case report and review of the literature</article-title><source>Dig Dis Sci</source><year>1993</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>185</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8420756</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Plail</surname><given-names>RO</given-names></name><name><surname>Bussey</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Glazer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Adenomatous polyposis: An association with carcinoma of the thyroid</article-title><source>Br J Surg</source><year>1987</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3036290</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>NR</given-names></name><name><surname>Cubilla</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Chaganti</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Association of endocrine neoplasia with multiple polyposis of the colon</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1983</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>1171</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6129922</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>WG</given-names></name><name><surname>Kern</surname><given-names>BB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The nature of the mutation in familial multiple polyposis: Papillary carcinoma of the thyroid, brain tumors and familial multiple polyposis</article-title><source>Dis Colon Rectum</source><year>1973</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>264</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4720000</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamilton</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bussey</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mendelsohn</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Diamond</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Pavlides</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Hutcheon</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Ileal adenomas after colectomy in nine patients with Adenomatous polyposis coli/Gardner&#x02019;s syndrome</article-title><source>Gastroenterology</source><year>1979</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>1252</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">499712</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>FI</given-names></name><name><surname>MacKinnon</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Papillary thyroid carcinoma associated with polyposis coli - A case of Gardner&#x02019;s syndrome</article-title><source>Am J Gastroenterol</source><year>1981</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>138</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7304549</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Keshgegian</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Enterline</surname><given-names>HT</given-nam